[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   Where does the intrinsic axis take over from the footprint?
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   For each semimajor-axis bin, count the fraction of objects
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   within +-60 deg of (a) the detached-cluster axis lam = 49 deg
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   and (b) the bin's OWN discovery-footprint mean direction.
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   Where pointing dominates, the footprint cap wins; where the
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   intrinsic structure dominates, the axis cap wins.  The
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   crossover radius is an empirical measurement of where the
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   boundary structure begins to organize the clock sector.
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   R1  Axis-score vs footprint-score in sliding a windows.
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   R2  Resonant control: Plutinos (3:2, a ~ 39.4 AU) have
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   perihelion longitudes pinned by resonance geometry, not
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   by any external axis or footprint.  Their axis-alignment
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   fraction is the natural control for the inner belt's
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   weak offset (b11).
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   R3  The sednoid subsample (a>150, q>50): the cleanest objects
[2026-09-20 10:42:16 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 017]   -- deepest boundary-residents -- for comparison.
